From a52687ade09870af95e7341f31a6f1ceda696acd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:36:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 267/275] fix(cuda): close six arch-selection fail-safe
 boundaries (r2)

Address the independent 0046/0047 boundary findings:

* sentinel-based constructor arguments: an explicitly supplied
  ptx_target/ptx_version is no longer confused with a default value.
  Explicit ptx_version must equal the pinned registry version exactly,
  so sm_120+8.0 and sm_120+8.8 fail at construction instead of being
  silently upgraded or failing later in compile();
* arch= is strictly mutually exclusive with explicit
  ptx_target/ptx_version (named 'cannot be combined' error, even when
  the values agree); unregistered ptx_target values are rejected
  (render_ptx remains the raw low-level entry point);
* malformed payload arch_selection values (string/int/null/list) now
  raise CudaPtxArtifactError instead of a raw ValueError/TypeError;
* the encoder refuses a non-default ptx_target/ptx_version without an
  arch_selection, so a hand-built CudaProgram cannot smuggle a native
  header through payload version 2; the decoder cross-checks the same
  invariant defensively and refuses v2 native headers;
* arch_selection is cross-checked against TargetSpec.attributes['arch']
  in validate() and in the decoder, so a re-signed target mutation is
  refused.

Default sm_80/PTX 8.0 artifacts stay byte-identical (payload digest
verified against pristine 2d6e87c7d).  Focused CUDA suite adds 9 tests
for these cases.
